<h6 id=3D"approximate-nearest-neighbor-ann">Approximate nearest neighbor (A=
NN)</h6>
<p>In many applications, it's sufficient to retrieve items that are similar=
 enough without needing to find the exact nearest neighbor. ANN algorithms =
use specialized data structures that allow the system to retrieve =E2=80=9C=
close enough=E2=80=9D neighbors without searching the entire dataset, thus =
reducing search time to sublinear complexity, for example, <span class=3D"k=
atex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Ma=
th/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>log<=
/mi><mo>=E2=81=A1</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=
=3D"false">)</mo><mo>=C3=97</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mr=
ow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(\log(N)\times D)</annotatio=
n></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"=
><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-=
align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-rig=
ht: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mop">l=
o<span style=3D"margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class=3D"mop=
en">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.10903e=
m;">N</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"=
margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class=3D"mbin">=C3=97</span><span cla=
ss=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class=
